ent-ShipbreakingFurnace = furnace
    .desc =
        High-temperature furnaces are used to dispose of and recycle light-alloy structures, aluminium frames, bulkheads and the like.

        Chunks of asteroid rock left in old freighters can be processed in them too.

        High temperatures are equally deadly to organics and electronics. Feeding nanocarbon or complex equipment to the furnace will destroy the item rather than recycle it.
ent-ShipbreakingProcessor = shipbreaking processor
    .desc =
        The processor is a chamber for the secondary recycling of carbon compounds.

        It is entirely unsuited to metals. Putting aluminium through the processor will not break the machine, but the sample will come out heavily contaminated and of little use for reuse.

        The processor chamber is lethal to cutters. Your carbon will be extracted, but you will not like it.
ent-ShipbreakingProcessorAdmeme = { ent-ShipbreakingProcessor }
    .desc = { ent-ShipbreakingProcessor.desc }
ent-ShipbreakingBarge = salvage barge
    .desc =
        The barge collects items that can be reused without full recycling.

        Electronics, furniture, containers, the complex assemblies of a ship: cutters are to drop all of it on the barge for later analysis and sorting by other Nakamura Engineering staff.
